T035 / quickstart scenario 8 / SC-013: the boot-selection state cannot be written from the slot
Hardware run by the operator on the BeagleBone Black, 2026-10-31. Timestamps are the host's.

Setup (as described by the operator)
- A bundle built from a working tree where /etc/fw_env.config pointed at 0xc0000 and 0xe0000 instead
  of 0x80000 and 0xa0000 (the gap before the first partition, so reads only). It carries the version
  54eaf72-dirty. U-Boot on the card is unchanged and still reads the real region.
- The board was running slot B (revision 005bca6, confirmed). The bundle was installed into slot A.

What the operator reported
1. Slot A booted three times, and the board reset each time (three reboots).
2. Each time U-Boot printed "OTA: booting slot A" with BOOT_A_LEFT going down, and ota-health reported
   the slot as not confirmed; fw_printenv printed a warning.
3. After the third attempt the board booted slot B on its own, and ota-status on B read as below.
   No console transcript of the three attempts was attached; points 1 and 2 are the operator's
   account, not a capture. The counts are therefore not shown here beyond "0 left" in the output.

ota-status on slot B after the rollback (captured):

[2026-10-31 10:46:10] # ota-status
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Running slot : B   revision 005bca6
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Confirmed    : yes, this boot passed its health check
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Next boot    : slot B (the running one)
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Boot order   : A B
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Slot A  /dev/mmcblk0p2
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     state     : RETIRED: it was tried and never confirmed, and is out of boot attempts
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     attempts  : 0 left, in the boot order: yes
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     installed : bundle 54eaf72-dirty, update number 1 (RAUC's record of the last write)
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Slot B  /dev/mmcblk0p3
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     state     : RUNNING, confirmed
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     attempts  : 3 left, in the boot order: yes
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     revision  : 005bca6 (this image's /etc/build-info)
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     installed : bundle 005bca6, update number 1 (RAUC's record of the last write)
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]
[2026-10-31 10:46:13] Health log   : /data/ota-health.log, 6 record(s); the last one:
[2026-10-31 10:46:13]     2026-10-31 03:33:56 UTC up=7s build=54eaf72-dirty slot=A condition=boot-state: NOT CONFIRMED: boot-selection state is unreadable (BOOT_A_LEFT)

What it shows
- The condition that failed is the fourth one, boot-state, with the variable named in the record.
  Scenario 8 expected exactly that; research on condition 2 (RAUC reading the same region) did not
  pre-empt it.
- The slot with the bad bundle was never confirmed (RETIRED, 0 attempts left), the device returned to
  slot B unaided, and the reason was read from /data after the reboot, by ota-status on B.
- Slot B kept its three attempts and is confirmed.

What it does not show
- The log has 6 records and only the last one is shown. Three attempts would give three records of
  this kind if nothing else wrote to it; what the other five are was not read. The file was not
  catted in full.
- The U-Boot line for each of the three attempts, and the watchdog reset time per attempt (not
  measured here; T034 holds the ~49 s figure).
- The warning text fw_printenv printed.
- The clock in the record (2026-10-31 03:33:56 UTC) is the device's floor plus uptime, not real time.
